{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.bar_invariant_total_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.bar_invariant_total_zero","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/FramingIsAChoice.lean#L107-L114","doc":"Consequently a self-conjugate state has zero **total** twist, hence weight\n`1`: it needs no framing convention at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.bar_invariant_forces_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.bar_invariant_forces_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/FramingIsAChoice.lean#L96-L105","doc":"**Where `T = 0` IS derivable: self-conjugate states.**\n\nThe bar involution negates the per-strand twist (`TwistDatum.bar`), so a state\nequal to its own conjugate satisfies `t = −t` pointwise, forcing `t = 0`. This\nis a real derivation of zero framing — on the bar-invariant sector only. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.exists_framing_pair_distinguished","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.exists_framing_pair_distinguished","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/FramingIsAChoice.lean#L89-L94","doc":"Sharper form: a **nontrivial** twist separates some pair of framings, so the\nprediction genuinely depends on the choice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.framing_unobservable_iff_trivial_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.framing_unobservable_iff_trivial_twist","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/FramingIsAChoice.lean#L72-L87","doc":"**The framing is unobservable exactly when the twist is trivial.**\n\nIf every framing gives the same weight then `θ = 1`; conversely `θ = 1` makes\nevery weight `1`. So at `θ ≠ 1` — i.e. `q ≠ 1`, the substrate regime — distinct\nframings give distinct predictions, and `T` must be fixed by a stated\nconvention. This is why `T = 0` cannot be a theorem of the ribbon axioms: they\nare precisely the axioms that leave `T` free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.zero_framing_is_weight_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.zero_framing_is_weight_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/FramingIsAChoice.lean#L68-L70","doc":"**`T = 0` is the \"no correction\" choice.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.framingWeight_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.framingWeight_zero","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/FramingIsAChoice.lean#L64-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.framingWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.FramingIsAChoice.framingWeight","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/FramingIsAChoice.lean#L60-L62","doc":"The ribbon weight of an integer framing, `θ ^ T`, in a commutative group of\nunits. ","signatureChunk":0}]}